Alpasim image build on the Scaleway cluster. Apply from the repo root:
    git -C py123d_garage/lib/alpasim/alpasim apply "$PWD/py123d_garage/.github/actions/alpasim_workspace/py123d_garage.patch"

Dockerfile: the CUDA base image from the NGC mirror, since Docker Hub resets
    connections from the compute nodes. Same image, same digest.
.dockerignore: copy uv.lock into the build context, so the image gets the versions
    setup_alpasim.sh resolved on the host instead of re-resolving the whole
    workspace, which needs GitHub. Upstream gitignores the lock, so it is per checkout.
Dockerfile: git protocol v1 inside the image, since v2 fetches fail on the cluster
    with "expected flush after ref listing".
Dockerfile: install every core package except alpasim_driver. The garage driver
    runs on the host, and the driver member is the only one installed from GitHub,
    which refuses anonymous fetches from the compute nodes.
src/controller/pyproject.toml: casadi<3.8. Not cluster specific: casadi 3.8.0
    dropped the casadi.tools re-exports do_mpc 5.1.1 imports, so the controller
    dies at import with any fresh resolution.
src/wizard/alpasim_wizard/services.py: no check of the docker GPU ids against
    nvidia-smi. Inside a Slurm job nvidia-smi only lists the allocated GPUs, while
    docker addresses GPUs by host index, so services.*.gpus=[<host index>] is
    right and the check rejected it.

